A||N||10||bHooper||4.3 liter v-6 for a S-10... swap???||||1||
Z||000000||bHooper||10-19-2000||10:01 AM||||yesterday, i stopped by the local AutoZone and was chatting with the manager about my car... about doing a 3.4 liter, next year.  when he said: "why not put a 4.3 liter in it?"<P>apparently this is a v-6 option for the S-10 pickup trucks.  does anyone know anything about these engines?<P>it sounds interesting.  will it mate to the getrag 5 speed?<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||loafer87gt||10-19-2000||10:03 AM||||From what I've read on this forum, you need the same kit and adapters as you need for a V8 kit to do the 4.3 swap. If your going to go to all the work to do a 4.3, why not just do a v8?||||reg||1
Z||000002||bHooper||10-19-2000||11:06 AM||||personnally, i would rather have the weight savings involved with a v-6 over a big block v-8.<P>does anyone know how much horsepower/torque a 4.3 v6 puts out?<P>which kit would you need?<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||LarryB||10-19-2000||11:29 AM||||Depends on the version, the late-80's ones without Vortec heads were rated at about 160HP.  The later Vortec-equipped versions are rated at around 190-200HP and 250-260 ft lbs depending on specific year and model.<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000004||lou_dias||10-19-2000||12:15 PM||||I've seen them go as high as 220hp from the factory...  it's eccentially a bored and stroked 3.8||||reg||1
Z||000005||bHooper||10-19-2000||12:18 PM||||so, you would need a 3.8 conversion kit, and wouldnt be able to use it with 5 speed?.<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000006||loafer87gt||10-19-2000||01:09 PM||||Correct me if I'm wrong, but isn't the 4.3 based off the v8 chevy smallblock, and not just a stroked 3.8? I thought it was basically a v8 with 2 less cylinders.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Raydar||10-19-2000||02:34 PM||||A 4.3 is 3/4 of a 350. Uses the Chevy trans bolt pattern. <BR>The earlier ones vibrated pretty badly. A balance shaft was added in 93-94. <BR>Several of us pestered Archie about adapting his V-8 kit to the 4.3 swap. I think he said he might try it out if he got the time. <BR>The 3.8 is probably as much bang for less bucks.    <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Hank is Here||10-19-2000||03:45 PM||||As far as I know the 4.3 is a V* with the front two cylinder chopped off, if I remember correct there was another Chevy 3.8 in the early 80's which was a 305 with the front two chopped off.  So the parts fellow is probably getting mixed up between a Buick and Chevy engine.  ||||reg||1
Z||000009||dman||10-19-2000||05:19 PM||||Hello everyone. Read these threads for more info about a 4.3 swap.<P>4.3 Vortec in a Fiero? <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/004756.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/004756.html</A>  <P>4.3L install update (long) <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/004874.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/004874.html</A>  <P>Based on what Squid has posted thus far, it seems like it would be easier than a V8; no special water pump system in the fender well, no custom harmonic balancer. Probably just an adapter plate, flywheel and some mounts to get it mated properly.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Fret Naught||10-20-2000||01:43 AM||||Hey Hoop!<BR>Got my ride back looks pretty good, I've been tossing around the engine swap now for some time, I think I have decided to go with the 3.4 and perhaps a turbo ta boot. never even considered a 4.3, from what I read there were too many mods for my blood. I like that drops right in uses the same harness mentality, I will be watching this thread to see what you find out.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FretNaught_sig_14.gif"> ||||reg||1
